        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-06T02:08:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As in, I\u0027m confused because the old interface only has one \u0027capability\u0027 here (value of supportsAmplitudeControl, CAP_AMPLITUDE_CONTROL). Should I really be adding all three of these? Or should it only be CAP_EXTERNAL_CONTROL and CAP_EXTERNAL_AMPLITUDE_CONTROL?",
      "parentUuid": "a0dc5739_76ee2189",
      "revId": "b3dacf28b30cebf0cdd8d4632be16496891d0cd3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0a3f0bb_40d5bba8",
        "filename": "vibrator/aidl/android/hardware/vibrator/IVibrator.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 101,
      "author": {
        "id": 1418133
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-06T02:23:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There should be three. Being single-purposed, it was reasonable for supportsAmplitudeControl() to be called in the context that setAmplitude() was to be used.\n\nFor example:\n\n// Normal operation, not using external control\nif (supportsAmplitudeControl()) {\n  setAmplitude();\n}\n\nif (supportsExternalControl()) {\n    setExternalControl(true);\n    // If external control is supported and enabled\n    if (supportsAmplitudeControl()) {\n      setAmplitude();\n    }\n}\n\nWe could require the same for getCapabilities(), but it would be at odds with how such APIs are generally used.",
      "parentUuid": "572030fc_31863fda",
      "revId": "b3dacf28b30cebf0cdd8d4632be16496891d0cd3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
